  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an array AAA of size NNN (1≤Ai≤1001 \\le A_i \\le 1001≤Ai​≤100), compute the number of triplets (i,j,k)(i, j, k)(i,j,k) satisfying the following conditions :\n\n\n1≤i,j,k≤N1 \\le i, j, k \\le N1≤i,j,k≤N\n∣Ai−Ak∣=∣i−j∣+∣j−k∣|A_i - A_k| = |i - j| + |j - k|∣Ai​−Ak​∣=∣i−j∣+∣j−k∣\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains NNN - the size of the array AAA\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,...ANA_1, A_2, ... A_NA1​,A2​,...AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of valid triplets.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤1001 \\le A_i \\le 1001≤Ai​≤100",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n5\n1 2 1 2 1\n3\n1 2 3\n4\n1 4 2 3",
        "output": "21\n17\n10",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 3 : The 101010 valid triplets are :\n\n(1, 1, 1)\n(1, 3, 2)\n(2, 2, 2)\n(2, 3, 1)\n(3, 3, 3)\n(3, 3, 4)\n(3, 4, 4)\n(4, 3, 3)\n(4, 4, 3)\n(4, 4, 4)"
      }
    ]
  },
